---
import { CLICKUP, MCP_MANUAL_PATH } from '@lib/compare/clickup-alternative';

const PROMPT =
  'Read the unresolved tasks in our ClickUp list “Web app”. Propose how each one maps to an issue in the ACME project: type, status, priority, assignee and tags. List likely duplicates. Create nothing until I approve the mapping.';
---

<section id="cu-switch" class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="cu-switch-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[680px]">
      <h2 id="cu-switch-title" class="h2">
        Moving your work across.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        There is no ClickUp importer. At launch there are two routes: a generic CSV import that works for any source,
        and an agent-assisted path for teams whose agent can reach both products. Both end with you reviewing the
        result.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 md:mt-14 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <article class="panel panel-pad" aria-labelledby="cu-csv-title">
        <p class="text-xs text-fg-2">Bulk, at launch</p>
        <h3 id="cu-csv-title" class="h3 mt-1">
          CSV import
        </h3>
        <ol class="steps-list mt-5 prose text-base">
          <li>Start from a CSV of the tasks you are moving.</li>
          <li>Map its columns to issue fields in the project you import into.</li>
          <li>Read the rows that could not be imported, with the reason for each, and fix them.</li>
          <li>Import. The result is ordinary issues you can search, plan and export again.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article class="panel panel-pad" aria-labelledby="cu-agent-title">
        <p class="text-xs text-fg-2">When your agent reaches both</p>
        <h3 id="cu-agent-title" class="h3 mt-1">
          Agent-assisted, with review
        </h3>
        <ol class="steps-list mt-5 prose text-base">
          <li>Connect one agent to ClickUp’s MCP server and to Nothing Left’s.</li>
          <li>Ask it to read the unresolved tasks and propose a mapping before it creates anything.</li>
          <li>Check the mapping, duplicates, attachments, history and who each person becomes.</li>
          <li>
            Approve. It creates projects, tags and issues and invites members through the MCP tools, as you, within your
            token’s scopes.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="quote mt-5">{PROMPT}</p>
        <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-xs">
          <li>
            <a class="link font-normal" href={CLICKUP.mcpConnect} rel="noopener">
              ClickUp: connect to its MCP server
              <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
                ↗
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="link font-normal" href={MCP_MANUAL_PATH}>
              Connect an agent to Nothing Left
              <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
                →
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
